{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517881-have-you-ever-created-a-detailed-backstory-for-character-ever-in-your-game","id":1517881,"title":"Have you ever created a detailed backstory for character ever in your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-13T09:25:46-07:00","id":1517881,"title":"Have you ever created a detailed backstory for character ever in your game?","content":"Just a fun question as I remember in the movie Collateral by Michael Mann that he had a notebook or something for hitman Vincent of where he was born and where he lived in what city at what age and how he became a mercenary and his interactions with the cabbie played by Jamie Foxx that showed more insights to why he is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T10:15:17-07:00","id":1517886,"title":"","content":"Absolutely NPCs/STCs as well I have about 40 or 50 NPCs in our Savage West San Fransisco forum &amp; about 20 in our Victorian London in-person campaign who all have at least a paragraph of background.<br /> <br /> Character wise we tend to write out maybe 50% of backstory as that adds helps with the character build and we leave 50% unwritten as that allows both the players and the ST to add thematic or just interesting elements.<br /> <br /> We have an Irish Fey blooded Mage with minor spheres in dreaming and naming, who is part of the Hempstock family (from Neil Gaimans Ocean at the end of the lane), the three sisters possibly being something connected to the Morrigan (which will evolve).<br /> He can continually see the dreaming whilst the other characters can\u2019t which creates both humorous and sinister moments in game.<br /> <br /> A young South Korean khan who is heavily patronised by the spirit court as well as beast courts, may have some spirit heritage hence the patronage but ends up accompanied by a motley crew of spirits who have displeased the Celestial bureaucracy and are sent to her in penance (they are of no help)<br /> <br /> Another is secretly a Unwilla (European wereowl) lived in Dorset England with his wife (who suffered completely from the delirium) until 1865 when she sadly passed.<br /> He moved to London and set up an antiques shop with a retainer who has followed the players character from game to game for 30 years, the character is the ancestor of one of his old modern day characters (a Child of Gaia killed by an abomination during the First War of Chicago) &amp; possessed some unusual gifts that cause paintings to come to life (ala the Old BBC show The Box of Delights) <br /> <br /> Some odd consistencies to iron out (Owl and werewolf) but that\u2019s part of the unwritten part of his character background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T10:19:04-07:00","id":1517887,"title":"","content":"And as this is a VTM thread applies equally to kindred STCs and players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T10:48:58-07:00","id":1517891,"title":"","content":"I don't tend to write a lot but I put a lot of thought in pcs and npcs. Simple stuff like their interests and hobbies with a consideration of their childhood helps a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> With pcs I go very deep. I could probably do a ama ic at this point lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T11:23:45-07:00","id":1517892,"title":"","content":"Yes.. to the point of overdoing it. About ten years ago or so I realized that I have almost more fun creating characters than playing them. When I ST this is fine, since most of it is confined to my folder and major NPCs have decent backgrounds and motivations. When I'm a player, it has been a problem. I just checked my last Vampire character (Tremere), and his character sheet is 48 pages long. CV, rituals, tools, paths, alchemy recipes, lineage, his studies and experiments, layout of the chantry and defenses, retainers (with their own character sheets), contacts, resources.. it's idiotically detailed and no ST ever would want to read all of that. Still had a blast making it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:06:12-07:00","id":1517896,"title":"","content":"I now try to keep character backstory to a half page at best. More than that, I found it doesn't help roleplay the character at all. It is just superfluous. And for most young vampires, it can probably be kept to the size of an index card.<br /> <br /> What I have found important is to create a detailed chronicle history. That will highlight the most important events of any NPCs in the city, and often create unexpected conflicts and interesting details. What were the critical events in the city's history, and who did what in them? Who were the Primogen for any length of time, and how were they removed, eliminated, or replaced? What important or curious mortal events were covers for vampire activity, and who did what during them? When did new characters enter the chronicle (either from embrace or travel from another domain), and how did that change things? If a character embraced another one, what kind of prestation did he need to pay - was that paid beforehand, or does he owe favors? Who in fact does owe prestation and to whom? Whom did the Prince destroy and for what reasons during his reign? What impact did that decision have? When were the important Blood Hunts called and for what reason, and what happened to the quarry?<br /> <br /> Figuring out those details will fill in more important details for characters than a backstory ever does. It does wonders for coterie charts and character interactions. And NPCs can then drop lots of bits of what happened during the important city events in conversations. You can overboard here too, but I find the time and effort well spent. <br /> <br /> Too often, events happen because they happen. Things are told in the passive voice. But by making history happen in the active voice by assigning specific people to do them, who helped them, and who opposed them, and the consequences of that; you end up creating a much more dynamic city. It doesn't seem static, and I found it seems to empower the PCs who think &quot;we can impact the city as well&quot;.<br /> <br /> For a PC, overly developed backstories are most often an excuse for players to claim a lot of false accomplishments that they won't ever try to do during game. A backstory should exist in order to provide context and justification for where you start in a chronicle, not be the culmination of that character's accomplishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T21:28:53-07:00","id":1517912,"title":"","content":"As much as it can be helpful to have a well fleshed out backstory for a character, I have learned that regardless of your best laid plans, the games will never go the way you expect them to. Which means excessive backstory is more often than not useless. The PCs will ignore the NPC with pages of backstory and fixate on the NPC that you added to a scene on the fly to flesh out a room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T22:14:45-07:00","id":1517916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517881-have-you-ever-created-a-detailed-backstory-for-character-ever-in-your-game?p=1517892#post1517892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.. to the point of overdoing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much<br /> I think most of the STs technically wrote a book series several dozen volumes long from the notes, backstories of PCs and NPC... just we not organized and publizied them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T00:37:57-07:00","id":1517925,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't, because the players will run roughshod all over my plans, but I do like to overthink things. Doesn't matter, the backstories are not for them, but for me (for enjoyment and improved roleplay). Characters tend to have a fleshed out backstory from childhood to embrace, several hobbies and notable life events, favourite [insert category here], and god help me when they're older than me because then I have to spend a week researching history to make sure I understand what their life was like and the events they've lived through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:17:11-07:00","id":1518084,"title":"","content":"Oh, <i>hell no</i>.<br /> <br /> You can't account for which NPC's your players will give a shit about, and what may or may not come up during a game even for the ones they do. In this, Murphy's law almost always prevails, and players inevitably glom onto whichever NPC you <i>didn't</i> put thought into before starting the chronicle, while ignoring (or eating) the ones you <i>did</i>.<br /> <br /> At most I throw together just enough to start the relationship map, and backfill <i>after</i> seeing in which characters my players are most invested. That way I tailor the story to what my players prefer, while leaving myself wiggle room to fart story beats and plot twists straight out of the luminiferous fucking aether if the story starts getting a little stale, and act like I've been the 4D chessmaster all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-15-2023, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:30:00-07:00","id":1518228,"title":"","content":"Would creating the family tree for several of my Nos characters count - with them all sharing a distant great-great-sire, and sharing some common flaws. Also having other branches of the tree that I can play in but have yet to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:38:11-07:00","id":1518535,"title":"","content":"I certainly would count that Babi_Gog and I have the start of a 4th generation Malkavian ancient that my character is a apart of on paper. So far it's just a name and the outlines of his backstory and what he is doing in the modern age. In this case he is trying to recall hazy moments of his mortal life and chunks of times that he can not account for since his embrace by Malkav.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-22-2023, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T06:45:07-07:00","id":1519168,"title":"","content":"Usually I create a character backstory not as a classical bio but school, medical and sometimes police files. That gives my storyteller (and players) some knowledge about my character abilities (apart from the character sheet). Also he can recall some main events which formed my character as flashbacks. As a ST i use the same metod, except that my players don't have typical character sheets but mentioned files. I create stats based on those data. That way PCs are more careful in their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 07-30-2023, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}